# GitHub status gate before push

Before every `git push` (and before `gh workflow run` that depends on Actions runners):

1. Check https://www.githubstatus.com/ (or `https://www.githubstatus.com/api/v2/summary.json`).
2. Inspect components that affect deploy/CI: **Actions**, **Git Operations**, **API Requests**, **Webhooks**.
3. If any of those is `degraded_performance`, `partial_outage`, or `major_outage`, **or** there is an unresolved incident mentioning Actions/deploy runners — **do not push**.

## What to do instead

- Keep the commit local (or commit only if the user asked for a commit).
- Tell the user GitHub is degraded and push is deferred.
- Prefer HostKey / SSH VPS hotfix for production emergencies (`HOST_KEY_API` → InvAPI → SSH), not a broken Actions deploy.
- Re-check status later; push only when Actions (and Git Operations) are `operational` again.

## Half-deploy / Actions stuck

Deploy already rolls back when `/health` does not become ready (`scripts/vps-deploy.sh`). That does **not** mean production is fine while Actions still shows Running/queued.

On any half-deploy, crash-loop, or 502/503 on `https://bot.themarfa.name/health`:

1. Inspect the live container immediately — `docker compose -f compose.vps.yml logs --tail=80 bot` (via HostKey/SSH). Do **not** wait for a green Actions run.
2. Fix or roll forward on the VPS; treat Actions UI as advisory during a GitHub outage.
3. Only after `/health` is `ok` (public + in-container) claim the bot is up.

## Missed live alerts after downtime

On restart the bot **already catch-up**s still-live streams (`check_streams` / went_live). Do **not** manually resend live alerts “just in case”.

Before any manual resend / force-notify:

1. Query prod (`scripts/vps-psql.sh`) — `alert_history` (DM) and/or `alert_delivery_log` (channel/group) for that `stream_id` / login since bot recovery.
2. Resend **only** rows that are still live on Twitch **and** have no delivery for this stream after the outage.
3. If catch-up already wrote history/log (~recovery time), leave them alone — a second send duplicates the user (as with snowboy_man / pen1ciodeltoro / sad_moustache).

## Why

A push to `main` triggers Deploy VPS. During Actions outages jobs stay `queued`/`in_progress` for a long time, half-deploy, or fail health checks while the live bot is already broken — prolonging downtime and confusing monitors.

## Exceptions

Only skip this gate if the user **explicitly** insists on pushing despite the outage after you warned them.

## Admin downtime alerts (PostHog)

Bot downtime often surfaces as PostHog Error Tracking `created` + `reopened` (or webhook retries). Admin Telegram notify is cooldown/deduped by issue fingerprint (see `notify_admins_posthog_issue` / `should_notify_posthog_issue`) so the same incident does not DM twice within ~45 minutes.
